# Never ship secrets into the build context.
#
# A bare `.env`/`.env.*` (no `**/` prefix) matches ONLY the context root —
# verified empirically (issue #150 review): Docker's own pattern matcher does
# NOT recurse a directory-less pattern the way `.gitignore` does. Every path
# below that needs to catch a nested workspace's own copy (apps/cms/.env,
# apps/storefront/.env.local, …) is written `**/…` for exactly that reason.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local file-backed build secrets (compose.production.yaml's BuildKit
# `awcms_api_token` secret, ADR-0019 D4) — never sent to a build context.
.secrets

# Reinstalled / rebuilt inside the image. `apps/storefront/Dockerfile`'s build
# stage COPYs the whole repo (see that file's own comment on why), which
# means the HOST's own `node_modules` — root and every workspace
# (apps/cms/node_modules alone is hundreds of MB) — would otherwise be sent
# into the build context and land OVER the image's freshly `bun install`ed
# one. `**/` is load-bearing here, not decorative: `node_modules/` alone was
# proven (issue #150 review) to exclude only a top-level `node_modules`, not
# `apps/cms/node_modules`.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.astro

# Not used to build, and copying them busts the source layer cache on every
# commit or note that changes. These are genuinely root-only in this repo (no
# nested `.git`/`.github`/`.claude`/`.changesets`), so a bare pattern is
# correct here — unlike `node_modules`/`dist`/`.env` above, which exist inside
# every workspace.
.git
.github
.claude
.changesets
docs/
*.md

# graphify skill output: analysis artefacts, not build inputs. Megabytes in
# size, and every rebuild of them busts the image's source layer cache.
# `apps/cms/graphify-out` is named explicitly because `apps/cms` has its own
# `.dockerignore` that this root one does not inherit or extend — a build
# from THIS root context reads only this file.
graphify-out/
apps/cms/graphify-out

# knowledge-graph federation docs (issue #11): human/agent reference, not a
# build input. `*.md` below already catches knowledge/curated/ and the
# generated notes; this line is explicit so the one non-.md file in there
# (knowledge/generated/graphify/graph.canvas) is caught too, deliberately
# rather than by the coincidence of a broader rule.
knowledge/

# tools/import-seputarborneo.ts's own output directory (git-ignored, can hold
# a legacy dump's exported row content) — never a build input.
tools/out

.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
**/*.log
